# Code Style and Architecture Patterns

Canon applies: the React documentation (rules of hooks, effects, keys), WAI-ARIA basics and the TypeScript handbook. Store internals are `mobx-store-template.mdc`; backend layering is `clean-architecture.mdc`. This rule holds only this project's frontend decisions.

## Rules

1. **`observer` on every component that reads an observable**, conditional reads included, as the outermost wrapper: `observer(withRouter(View))`. A component that reads only props needs none.
2. **Layers.** A service does IO only; a store holds state, logic and state transitions; a component renders and forwards events to store actions. No API/IO call and no business logic (validation, transformation, branching on domain state) in a component, its handlers or its effects.
3. **Where state lives.** UI-only state that one component uses (an open flag, a hover, an input draft) is `useState`. State with logic, or read by another component or a store, lives in a store; it is never copied into `useState`. `useMemo`/`useCallback` do not wrap store values or store methods.
4. **A store is created once per mount**: `useState(() => new PageStore(api))[0]` or `useLocalObservable`, never `new Store()` in the component body.
5. **An effect that subscribes, listens or starts a timer returns its cleanup.** Data loading is not started from an effect (see `mobx-store-template.mdc` Rule 8).
6. **List keys** are on the element `.map()` returns and are stable ids; an index key only for a static list that never reorders or filters.
7. **Accessibility.** `<img>` has `alt` (`""` when decorative); an icon-only button or link has `aria-label`; a form input has a label; a clickable element is a `<button>` or `<a>`, not a `<div onClick>`.
8. **TypeScript.** No `any` (use `unknown` and a guard, or the named type). A `!` assertion carries a comment that proves it; otherwise use `?.`/`??` and handle the missing case. Props types are `XProps`, no `I` prefix. Imports use relative paths or the configured aliases, never `from "src/..."`.

---

## Review severities (shared with reviewers)

`review-frontend` rates these patterns by this table. Change a row here, never in a reviewer.

| Signal | A finding when | Default | Not a finding |
|---|---|---|---|
| Component reads observables without `observer` (Rule 1) | always | `major` (the UI does not update when the observable changes) | a component that reads only props |
| `observer` inside another HOC (Rule 1) | always | `minor`; `major` with a named defect | — |
| API/IO or business logic in a component (Rule 2) | always | `minor`; `major` with a named defect it causes or a stated project rule | — |
| Shared or store-owned state kept in `useState`, or copied from a store (Rule 3) | two owners of the value can diverge, named | `major` | UI-only state one component uses |
| `useMemo`/`useCallback` around a store value or method (Rule 3) | always | `minor` | a memo over values that are not store state |
| Store constructed in the component body (Rule 4) | always | `major` (recreated on each render, state lost) | `useState(() => new Store())`, `useLocalObservable` |
| Subscription, listener or timer without cleanup (Rule 5) | always | `major` | — |
| Missing `key` (Rule 6) | always | `major` | — |
| Index key on a list that reorders, filters or paginates (Rule 6) | always | `minor` | a static list |
| `<img>` without `alt`; interactive element without an accessible name (Rule 7) | always | `major` | — |
| Clickable non-semantic element without keyboard support (Rule 7) | always | `minor` | — |
| `!` on a value the types allow to be missing (Rule 8) | a named input reaches it | `blocker` when it throws during render; `major` elsewhere; `minor` with no input shown | a `!` with a comment that proves it |
| `any` in new code (Rule 8) | always | `minor`; `major` with a named input and the wrong value it lets through | — |
| `I`-prefixed props type, `from "src/..."` import (Rule 8) | introduced by the change | `minor` | — |
